-- title:
--   Flat base change of torsion bounds for a two-term complex
-- statement:
--   Let $R_0$ be a commutative ring and $R$ a commutative $R_0$-algebra that is flat as an $R_0$-module. Let $L_0, C_0, D_0$ be $R_0$-modules and let $u_0 \colon L_0 \to C_0$, $d_0 \colon C_0 \to D_0$ be $R_0$-linear with $d_0(u_0 x) = 0$ for all $x \in L_0$. Let $J \subseteq R_0$ be an ideal such that (i) every $x$ with $u_0 x = 0$ satisfies $a \cdot x = 0$ for all $a \in J$, and (ii) for every $y$ with $d_0 y = 0$ and every $a \in J$ there is $x \in L_0$ with $u_0 x = a \cdot y$. Let $L, C, D$ be $R$-modules, $u \colon L \to C$ and $d \colon C \to D$ be $R$-linear, and let $e_L \colon R \otimes_{R_0} L_0 \simeq L$, $e_C \colon R \otimes_{R_0} C_0 \simeq C$, $e_D \colon R \otimes_{R_0} D_0 \simeq D$ be $R$-linear isomorphisms compatible with $u$ and $d$ on elements $1 \otimes x$, in the sense that $u(e_L(1 \otimes x)) = e_C(1 \otimes u_0 x)$ for all $x \in L_0$ and $d(e_C(1 \otimes y)) = e_D(1 \otimes d_0 y)$ for all $y \in C_0$. Then, writing $JR$ for the image ideal $J \cdot R$ generated by the image of $J$ under $R_0 \to R$: every $x \in L$ with $u x = 0$ satisfies $a \cdot x = 0$ for all $a \in JR$, and for every $y \in C$ with $d y = 0$ and every $a \in JR$ there is $x \in L$ with $u x = a \cdot y$. Both conclusions are stated elementwise rather than as equalities of submodules.
--
--   This is the two-term-complex form of the assertion that an annihilation bound on $\ker u_0$ and an exponent bound for the failure of exactness at $C_0$ are preserved under flat base change, the ideal $J$ being replaced by its extension to $R$. It is used in the sheaf-theoretic layer, by [`AlgebraicGeometry.OModulePresheaf.forall_smul_eq_zero_and_exists_eq_smul_of_le_of_flat_of_bijective`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.OModulePresheaf.forall_smul_eq_zero_and_exists_eq_smul_of_le_of_flat_of_bijective), to transport such uniform torsion bounds along a flat base change of presheaves of modules.
